#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
perfp -- perf preprocessor for Ascend simulator profiling dumps.

Reads the ``visualize_data.bin`` container produced by MindStudio / msInsight,
splits it into its logical records, and emits an AI-agent friendly analysis
bundle:

    out/
      README.md                 how to use this bundle
      summary.md                human / LLM readable digest
      summary.json              machine readable digest
      schema.sql                SQLite DDL
      queries.sql               example queries
      profile.sqlite            queryable database (dictionary encoded)
      csv/                      exported tables (aggregates + event stream)
      src/                      embedded source files (kernel + CANN headers)
      raw/trace.json.gz         the original trace timeline, losslessly kept
      raw/records/*.json        the small non-trace records, raw

Only the Python standard library is used (sqlite3, json, gzip, csv, ...).

Container format (reverse engineered, validated by walking the whole file):

    record header, 12 bytes, little endian:
        u32 payload_len | u32 reserved(0) | u8 type | u8 subtype | 2 magic bytes
    payload_len bytes of payload
    for type == 1 (embedded source file) a further 4096 bytes of padding

Known record types for this producer:
    1  embedded source file   payload = "path\0" + NUL padding + file content
    2  Chrome Trace Event JSON (``traceEvents``)
    3  Files table   (per source line, 38-core arrays)
    4  Instructions  (2354 static instructions, 38-core arrays) + schema
"""

